{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540263-the-priesthood-of-the-obfuscating-eclipse-moros-prime-death-homebrew-legacy","id":1540263,"title":"The Priesthood of the Obfuscating Eclipse - Moros Prime/Death homebrew legacy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-12T22:51:41-07:00","id":1540263,"title":"The Priesthood of the Obfuscating Eclipse - Moros Prime/Death homebrew legacy","content":"<br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Priesthood of the Obfuscating Eclipse</span></u><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Eclipse Clerics</span></i><br /> <br /> The history of the legacy is, appropriately, obfuscated behind layers of misdirection, false information, and half-truths to the point where even the modern masters of this legacy do not know its true origins or history. It is believed to have formed in antiquity, perhaps in Persia, Greece, or Egypt, but some claim that it formed after the Roman Empire adopted Christianity, and still others claim that it formed during the crusades. The only thing that is agreed upon is that the legacy formed when a group of Moros, rarely considered to be a cabal, came together under a solar eclipse to perform a Supernal summoning. It is unknown if these Moros were servants of the Father, or if they summoned a specter that was aligned with the Exarch by accident. Whatever the case, <i>Eclipsed Truth</i> appeared before them, and when the Moros left, the Priesthood of the Obfuscating Eclipse was formed. These Eclipse Clerics had shaped their souls with the help of the Stygian shade to fulfill the work of The Father, hiding the Truth.<br /> <br /> It is important to note two facts, or really the lack thereof, when it comes to the origin story of this legacy. Firstly, many Seers of the Throne claim that the mages who founded the Priesthood of the Obfuscating Eclipse were also Seers who served the Father actively and consciously but there is no evidence for this, it is just as likely that the Moros that had gathered under the eclipse that day were all Banishers, trying to find a way to hide the mysteries from sleepers and thus have less awakened in the world. Secondly, the truth of the eclipse is not known. Those who have summoned Eclipsed Truth since then claim that the sun is blocked out by its presence, so it is unclear if the eclipse was already happening when the summoning was being done, or if it began after the shade had been summoned.<br /> <br /> Whatever the case, the Priesthood persists into the modern era. Its ranks are primarily filled with Seers of the Paternoster Ministry, but ideological banishers also join the legacy, albeit in much smaller numbers. While the Seers see the nameless Banishers as thieves of this legacy they rarely strike out against them, instead they see them as useful tools, as they go about the fallen world doing the Father's work without ever asking for help or resources, leaving the Seers to handle more important works. The only true issue the Seers have with these Banishers are that they tend to get caught by the Pentacle more often, and as such the secrets of the legacy are more likely to fall into the hands of the Pentacle because of this. This has led the Pentacle to believe that this is strictly a legacy of Banishers, so when all the damage is added up, the Seers are quite okay with the results.<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Most mages who come to this legacy have a history in religious or occult organizations that emphasize secrecy, even from its fellow members. Trust is something to never be fully given in those spaces, and it tends to serve them well as an Eclipse Cleric.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance: </b>The Priesthood the Obfuscating Eclipse tend to dress mundanely as to not draw attention to themselves. Many are leaders of a religious group and dress appropriately for that, but otherwise you would never think twice about seeing them walking down the street.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> Top down, with<i> Eclipsed Truth </i>being seen as the true leader of the legacy, but in practice those mages that have mastered the legacy's attainments lead, and those who still must learn follow.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory:</b> The mages of this legacy believe that magic should be hidden from all, sleeper and awakened alike, and their magic facilitates this. The Eclipse Clerics are still mages and therefore still obsessive, and tend to take a \u201cnone for you, all for me\u201d mindset when it comes to who should be experiencing magic, and even then only if it is part of one of their obsessions. They will even hide magic from other Seers of the Throne. These mages see the sun as the greatest symbol of the Truth, with light representing smaller pieces. You can, and should, snuff out a candle but the sun will always shine, so it is best to block it as best you can. However, when it comes to the awakened, each carries a light within themselves, the soul, and that light should be snuffed out.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Doctrine and Magic</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Moros<br /> <b>Parent Order:</b> The Paternoster Ministry or sometimes Ideological Banishers<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Prime 2, Death 1, Subterfuge 2, one of the following additional skills at 2 dots or higher: Investigation, Larceny, Occult, Persuasion,<br /> <b>Initiation:</b> Summon the <i>Eclipsed Truth</i> and study its symbolism.<br /> <b>Ruling Arcana:</b> Prime<br /> <b>Yantras: </b>Casting under a solar eclipse (+1 for a partial eclipse, +3 for a full eclipse); Veils (+1); Casting magic that only they are aware of (+2); Obscuring a light source (+1)<br /> <b>Oblations: </b>Keeping a secret; Successfully hiding magic from someone searching for it; Destroying light sources, magical or mundane.<br /> <br /> <b>Attainments</b><br /> The attainments of the legacy are not taught but mages, the members of the legacy are discouraged from creating soul stones, and creating a Daimonomikon is punishable by death. The only way mages should learn the attainments is by summoning <i>Eclipsed Truth</i> and studying it.<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment: First Contact</b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:9px\">Prerequisites: Initiation</span></i><br /> Working in the shadow and darkness is the mission of the Eclipse Clerics, and that is a difficult task when you pick the wrong fight with the wrong mage, especially one more powerful than you. The first lesson taught by this legacy is how to identify the power of the mage who has left behind their magical mark. When scrutinizing the signature nimbus of another mage they may activate this attainment, which functions as \u201cNimbus Tuning\u201d (Prime 1, SoS 94) with reach for instant casting.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Death 1</span></i><br /> Darkness obfuscates, but not from the Eclipse Clerics. This attainment allows the mage to see in non-magical darkness without penalty. The attainment has advanced duration and takes one hour of meditation for it to take effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment: Penumbra</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>Prerequisites: Prime 2, 3 dots in Subterfuge</i></span><br /> The Priesthood of the Obfuscating Eclipse\u2019s primary goal is hiding magic, and they use this attainment to bring about this goal from early in their training. This attainment functions as \u201cSupernal Veil\u201d (Prime 2, MtAw 168) with reach for advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>Optional: Death 2</i></span><br /> The Eclipse Clerics must be able to identify and differentiate between mages and non-mages, as well as identifying how powerful the mage is. Picking the correct target to interfere with is an important part of the Eclipse Cleric\u2019s job, and this attainment assists in that task. The attainment functions like \u201cSoul Marks\u201d (Death 1, MtAw 128) with reach for instant casting and sensory casting.<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment: Partial Eclipse</b><br /> <br /> <i>Prerequisites: Prime 3, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 3 or a second option from the list must be raised to 2</i><br /> Some mysteries are too well known for the Eclipse Clerics to simply tuck away, but they can obfuscate the details of the mystery, sending those who study it down false paths. This attainment functions like the spell \u201cPath to Jerusalem\u201d (Prime 2, SoS 28) with reach for advanced duration and the bonus reach effect allowing them to plant false pieces of information in the mystery, or hiding true pieces.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Death 3</span></i><br /> In order to hide magic, the members of this legacy also learn to hide themselves from the sight of mages, blending in with the sea of sleepers. The attainment functions as \u201cSuppress Aura\u201d (Death 2, MtAw 129) with reach for advanced duration and instant casting. <br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment: A Darkened Sky</b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Prerequisites: Prime 4, 4 dots in Subterfuge</span></i><br /> Eclipse Clerics can return the veil of darkness in each sleepers soul to sleepwalkers, darkening their eyes to the Truth. This attainment is withstood by the resolve of the sleepwalker target. Should the withstand be bypassed the sleepwalker becomes a sleeper for the duration of the attainment. The attainment has reach for both advanced duration and instant casting and the primary factor for the attainment is potency.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>Optional: Death 4</i></span><br /> Darkness is a tool of the Eclipse Clerics, and with this attainment that becomes literal. The attainment functions like \u201cShadow Crafting\u201d (Death 3, MtAw 132) with reach for advanced duration and instant casting.<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment: Totality</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>Prerequisites: Prime 5, The optional skill used to meet the requirements of initiation must be raised to 4 or a second option from the list must be raised to 3 or a third option must be raised to 2</i></span><br /> The Eclipse Clerics can end nearly all spells they come across, only the spells of masters are safe from this attainment.\u200b After meditating for an hour near a spell they wish to end, the mage spends one mana to activate this attainment, which functions like \u201cSupernal Dispellation\u201d (Prime 4, MtAw 170) with the reach effect to make the attainment\u2019s effects lasting.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Optional: Death 5</span></i><br /> It is said that mages who have mastered all the attainments of the Priesthood of the Obfuscating Eclipse do not exist. This is not true, but one must become a master of the legacy in order to know this, and it is all because of this attainment. The attainment costs one mana to activate, along with one hour of mediation. It copies the effect of \u201cEmpty Presence\u201d (Death 5, MtAw 133) with reach for advanced duration. \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26284,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","user":"Aendrinastor","date":". 11-09-2024, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T22:54:27-07:00","id":1540264,"title":"","content":"Suh<br /> Preping for my game I was thinking about a Banisher character who's whole deal is about hiding magic until it can be destroyed, and as I thought more and more about this character, it morphed into a legacy about doing just that. Originally it was meant to be for banishers, but it felt like it fit into the themes of The Paternoster Ministry and the Father, so I took it in a direction that fit both.<br /> <br /> Obviously its not yet done, still need to name the attainments, and need to figure out what that third optional attainment for Death is gonna be, but I'm happy with it and looking forward to getting to use it in my game with an NPC at some point here. although its just occured to me that i'm going to have to change the MO of the NPC some to fit the legacy he is a part of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T13:19:45-07:00","id":1540287,"title":"","content":"Would it be accurate to say they are focused on hiding an item until it can be acquired or destroyed ? I am not sure since <i>Deepen Shadows</i> and <i>Sever the Awakened Soul</i> don't seem to match that. Especially the last, since a mage without a soul is a living Paradox risk. Maybe the first optional could plunder a rote from a subject's soul, but that would require them to be careful identifying Warped or Befouled rotes. Maybe the main Attainment could detect them, after all, Prime can see into the soul to write down a rote into a Grimoire.<br /> <br /> Another possible approach could be using Mind and Death, building on the idea of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_PmJbete83M\" target=\"_blank\">antimemetics</a>, an offshoot of the <i>Logophages</i> that fights cognitohazards, making them not only difficult to remember, but also impossible to describe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-13-2024, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T16:41:10-07:00","id":1540312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540263-the-priesthood-of-the-obfuscating-eclipse-moros-prime-death-homebrew-legacy?p=1540287#post1540287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be accurate to say they are focused on hiding an item until it can be acquired or destroyed ? I am not sure since <i>Deepen Shadows</i> and <i>Sever the Awakened Soul</i> don't seem to match that. Especially the last, since a mage without a soul is a living Paradox risk. Maybe the first optional could plunder a rote from a subject's soul, but that would require them to be careful identifying Warped or Befouled rotes. Maybe the main Attainment could detect them, after all, Prime can see into the soul to write down a rote into a Grimoire.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the goal, yes I can't find a way to fit the the final Death attainment into it unless I include souls into the idea, I honestly forgot about the paradox problem, <i>but</i> I do like this idea of deleting rotes, or maybe Praxis, from someone...will think on that.<br /> <br /> As for Deepen Shadow attainment, the idea there was to draw on the idea of the eclipse and darkening the light (Truth) in the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540263-the-priesthood-of-the-obfuscating-eclipse-moros-prime-death-homebrew-legacy?p=1540287#post1540287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another possible approach could be using Mind and Death, building on the idea of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_PmJbete83M\" target=\"_blank\">antimemetics</a>, an offshoot of the <i>Logophages</i> that fights cognitohazards, making them not only difficult to remember, but also impossible to describe.</div> </div> </div> </div>An incognito attainment could be cool, will have to think on that as well.<br /> <br /> Ty for directional help here! will return when I've made some progress","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T16:42:50-07:00","id":1540313,"title":"","content":"Oh, the idea behind the soul snatching stuff is that Mages carry a bit of the Truth in their soul and the Eclipse Clerics wanna snuff that shit out, but, like I said, I forgot about the paradox risk and I'm not sure these guys would be okay with that at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T07:00:42-07:00","id":1540351,"title":"","content":"This would be an exceptionally non-standard design, but could the final Death Attainment symbolically &quot;kill&quot; the truth within the Mage, undoing their Awakened state? It does sound like the logical endpoint for Priesthood's dogma. I assume the effect would be Lasting, but a demanding quest could reconnect the victim with the Supernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T08:02:10-07:00","id":1540357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540263-the-priesthood-of-the-obfuscating-eclipse-moros-prime-death-homebrew-legacy?p=1540351#post1540351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be an exceptionally non-standard design, but could the final Death Attainment symbolically &quot;kill&quot; the truth within the Mage, undoing their Awakened state? It does sound like the logical endpoint for Priesthood's dogma. I assume the effect would be Lasting, but a demanding quest could reconnect the victim with the Supernal.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like a variant of the Timori's Gnosis eating ? Maybe the quest or killing the cleric could restore their Gnosis, adding a layer of challenge to using it effectively.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking that, since <i>Stealing Fire</i> is a Perfecting of Prime, a Fraying should allow a Sleepwalker to be temporarily made into a Sleeper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T13:00:35-07:00","id":1540382,"title":"","content":"I wasn't actually thinking abut the Timori, since they weren't officially adapted to 2ed rules, but yes. The Attainment could suppress all of Gnosis in one go, remove one Dot per casting, or apply a curse that gradually reduced Gnosis as if the subject suffered from soul loss. Making the death of the Cleric into the cure would have an interesting psychological effect on the Legacy. Each use would paint a target of the practitioner's back, that they would have to justify to themselves.<br /> <br /> Reversed <i>Stealing Fire</i> would be <i>mean</i>, but thematically appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-17T17:22:21-07:00","id":1540598,"title":"","content":"There is a boon that Angels of Death get in SoS that let them lower gnosis by their rank, that could work, lowering gnosis for the duration of that attainment, which at the capstone is a year, make them into a sleepwalker if they have gnosis 4 or less, or just do the quest idea like you're talking about, those could work<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T14:43:09-07:00","id":1540658,"title":"","content":"A few ideas for Attainment names, based on the themes and on the abilities to obscure the connection to the Supernal:<br /> <br /> Tenebrous Revelation<br /> Umbral Surplice<br /> Obscuring Saeta<br /> Halo of Annulus<br /> Sunless Procession","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-18T16:24:52-07:00","id":1540663,"title":"","content":"I've gone ahead and removed the optional Death attainments from attainments 3-5 until I figure out something I'm more excited about. I know I wanna use Death to hit on the theme of darkness, I have some ideas and once I've sat on them for a few days I'll decide if I like them or not and come back for feedback.<br /> <br /> I went ahead and changed the fourth Prime attainment because I really like the idea of turning sleepwalkers into sleepers for this legacy, thats a good idea tyvm for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T18:35:50-07:00","id":1541010,"title":"","content":"So im not 100% sure how I feel about the Death Attainments but i've given them a second go, focusing on darkness and hiding their presence","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-25T18:37:56-07:00","id":1541012,"title":"","content":"Might have to rework their written lore a bit to accomidate the final optional attainment but we'll see","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T00:55:29-07:00","id":1541014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1540263-the-priesthood-of-the-obfuscating-eclipse-moros-prime-death-homebrew-legacy#post1540263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Fourth Attainment: A Darkened Sky</b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Prerequisites: Prime 4, 4 dots in Subterfuge</span></i><br /> Eclipse Clerics can return the veil of darkness in each sleepers soul to sleepwalkers, darkening their eyes to the Truth. This attainment is withstood by the resolve of the sleepwalker target. Should the withstand be bypassed the sleepwalker becomes a sleeper for the duration of the attainment. The attainment has reach for both advanced duration and instant casting and the primary factor for the attainment is duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>This could be a feature or a bug, but since the Primary Factor is Duration, Potency of this Attainment can't exceed 3 (considering additional spell factors). This means that the Attainment only works on Sleepwalkers with Resolve 1 or 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-26T10:07:56-07:00","id":1541023,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\">I was thinking more about the theme of obfuscating the Supernal without inviting the Abyss, how the Paternoster might want to take full advantage of Disbelief and how it might also affect their Death Attainments. How about a </span>Potency primary Making of Death and Prime that combines <i>Eidolon </i>with an <i>Avernian Gate</i>, creating a sentient fog with water from the Ocean of Fragments (think the angel of death from <i>Prince of Egypt</i>). Its field is finding and consuming memories of the eclipse cleric's choice, meaning not even Awakened are safe now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Reach could be assigned to advanced duration and a mana is used to pay for [lowest of Death and Prime] charges, with mana needing to be refilled normally afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-26-2024, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-27T07:26:29-07:00","id":1541060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong>